From: Maksim Sisov <msisov@igalia.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:48:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/48] profiles: Depend on //extensions/browser with
 extensions core

On desktop Android, where enable_extensions_core is true but
enable_extensions is false, a clean build can fail to compile
profile.cc with "'extensions/common/mojom/manifest.mojom-shared.h'
file not found". This closed the tree on
android-desktop-arm64-archive-rel.

profile.cc includes //extensions/browser headers under
ENABLE_EXTENSIONS_CORE since https://crrev.com/c/6489846, but the
"profile" target only depends on //extensions/browser when
enable_extensions is set. The generated mojom headers are thus not
ordered before the compile, and the build passes only when another
target happens to generate them first.

Fix by adding the dependency under enable_extensions_core.

Bug: 553138801
Test: Build profile.o alone in a fresh desktop Android out dir
Change-Id: Ia860b5b442e7fc0d4cd25b3d22b745c2a11930fc
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8525567
Owners-Override: Ritika Gupta <ritikagup@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Ritika Gupta <ritikagup@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Sky Malice <skym@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Ritika Gupta <ritikagup@google.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1712591}
(cherry picked from commit 06464c2236ae7c849d9a32df41da63673960ce5c)
---
 chrome/browser/profiles/BUILD.gn | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/profiles/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/profiles/BUILD.gn
index 1c4ee4ac17..09af93b511 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/profiles/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/profiles/BUILD.gn
@@ -423,7 +423,7 @@ source_set("profile") {
     "//content/public/browser",
     "//extensions/buildflags",
   ]
-  if (enable_extensions) {
+  if (enable_extensions_core) {
     deps += [ "//extensions/browser" ]
   }
   if (is_chromeos) {
